"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d37\"},\"ref\":\"d37\",\"snippet\":\" ... A selection of his poetry is collected in Desire Never … Read More\\n\\nColm Toíbín\\n\\nColm Toíbín is the author of six novels, including The Master, winner of the International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award and shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize, as well as winner of the LA Times ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d38\"},\"ref\":\"d38\",\"snippet\":\" ... Exploring the World of Reading Books\\n\\nWomen's Prize for Fiction - High-profile literary awards in 2024\\n\\n6. International Dublin Literary Award\\n\\nA famous international literary award, the International Dublin Literary Award was founded in 1996 and is given out every year to a novel written in English ... \",\"title\":\"https://blueroseone.com/publish/list-of-15-most-prestigious-literary-awards-in-2024/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Known World won the Pulitzer Prize for Fiction in 2004 and the International Dublin Literary Award in 2005.\\n\\nEdward P. Jones is an award-winning American author and short story writer. His first short story collection, Lost in the City, won the PEN/Hemingway Award and was ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d39\"},\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... His 2001 novel The Corrections drew widespread critical acclaim, earned Franzen a National Book Award, was a Pulitzer Prize for Fiction finalist, earned a James Tait Black Memorial Prize, and was shortlisted for the International Dublin Literary Award. His novel Freedom (2010) garnered similar praise and led to ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonathan_Franzen\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"fce17780df98c17cebd43edaabfb66de95d18eea5a9747cab465cee25af664df\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"6931b0b80def24ed210baf0dbf5436ac4e78ee684107e7b2e44b175312b09970\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Dublin Literary Award founded 1996 winner 2010s\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_2e061b341a3d4e2d912f610c"},{"content":"I found a strong lead: Chigozie Obioma's novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages. Let me investigate this further. The Booker Prize was created in 1969, but the puzzle says the award was created in the 2000s. Let me check the Man Booker International Prize (created 2005) and verify the details.\n\nLet me read the Obioma page and search for more details.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d30\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_4fb942867c984fdbb79081e7","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma born grew up city biography\", \"An Orchestra of Minorities 2019 Man Booker International Prize shortlist\", \"The Fishermen 2015 Booker Prize shortlist translated languages\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_df14c0ccecd3421385ef1120","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d30\",\"document_chars\":17355,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"79767844ce2071fc5dcf3fb0e64d0cade0ba154ef0fc324d0054c1c767e63138\",\"snapshot\":\"90019ca46504785f620ef12f36abae20080c8c3bc7809053339e4beaa4deb2fd\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: ADVISORS\\ndate: 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was named one of Foreign Policy's 100 Leading Global Thinkers in 2015 and served as a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Distinguished Professor of English and Creative Writing at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Writers retreat. His third novel, The Road to the Country, was published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nRosie is a production and event manager based in Athens, Greece, with extensive experience in coordinating high-profile film festivals and cultural events. She holds a degree in Communication, Media and Culture from Athens and pursued further studies in Art History in Paris, culminating in a Master's in Culture & Tourism from Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne. Her professional experience includes collaborations with cultural organizations and festivals worldwide, including UNESCO in New York, the Rolex Art Festival, Les Rencontres d'Arles Photo Festival among others. Since 2018, she has served as Festival Coordinator and Special Events Manager for the French Film Festival of Greece, and since 2022, she has been the Head of Production for the Athens International Children's Film Festival. Driven by a deep passion for cultural engagement and sustainable tourism, she continually seeks innovative ways to connect communities through the arts. In her free time, she enjoys playing music and gardening.\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Professor of Creative Writing and English at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Fiction Writers program. His third novel, The Road to the Country, will be published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nKaterina Papanikolopoulos joined Faliro House in 2022 as Manager of Special Projects – a position that evolved into her role acting as the 2024 Oxbelly Retreat, Fiction Writers Program Manager. Following her graduation from UCLA (Summa Cum Laude, Art History), Papanikolopoulos founded the non-profit Athens Design Forum (ADF), a platform that advocates for overlooked and generative design histories interwoven with global labor and migration pa\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_4fb942867c984fdbb79081e7"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d25\"},\"ref\":\"d25\",\"snippet\":\" ... Farrell\\n*Karen Joy Fowler\\n*Linda Grant\\n*Abdulrazak Gurnah\\n*Sarah Hall\\n*Mohsin Hamid\\n*Shirley Hazzard\\n*Philip Hensher\\n*Mary Lawson\\n*David Lodge\\n*Patrick McCabe\\n*Colum McCann\\n*Tom McCarthy\\n*Shena Mackay\\n*Chigozie Obioma\\n*Michael Ondaatje\\n*Joseph O'Neill\\n*Tim Parks\\n*Caryl Phillips\\n*Julian Rathbone\\n*Mordecai Richler\\n*Arundhati Roy\\n*Bernice Rubens\\n*Donal ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma\\ndate: 2000-01-01\\n---\\n-\\n\\n- MajorsMinorsCertificates\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Policies & ProceduresFYW Guidebook\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Digital Learning LabsPortfoliosEvaluationsMoran ePortfolio AwardsBarnett Essay AwardsDouble Dawgs\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Transfer FAQProspective Student Information\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Study AbroadInternships and Research Opportunities\\n\\n>>\\n\\n-\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Double DawgsTransfer Student InformationDual Degree Progra\",\"title\":\"https://www.english.uga.edu/directory/people/chigozie-obioma\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\" ... This book brilliantly explores the effects of slavery and colonialism on African families as the story unfolds between West Africa and the United States.\\n\\n- The Fishermen (2015) by Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): In this heartbreaking tale, four brothers in a small Nigerian town have their lives turned upside down ... \",\"title\":\"https://enkoeducation.com/the-must-read-in-african-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... Appiah argues that, unlike their counterparts who grew up facing the crudest forms of racial and colonial discrimination in the West and the Francophone subcontinent, the likes of S̩óyinká were \\\"children who were extracted from the traditional culture of their parents and grandparents and thrust into the ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2019/04/why-im-no-longer-talking-to-nigerians-about-race\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma, in The Orchestra of Minorities does the same. You shall notice in my next novel, The Wanderers [to be published in April/May], that I delve into this a little deeper also, to depict the notion of the absurdity of the human condition, which though popularized ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2021/03/the-xhosa-literary-revival\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... Purple Hibiscus (2003), Half of a Yellow Sun (2006), Americanah (2013)\\n* Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): The Fishermen (2015), An Orchestra of Minorities (2019)\\n* José Eduardo Agualusa (Angola): Rainy Season, Creole, The Book of Chameleons, My Father's Wives\\n* Ama Ata Aidoo (Ghana): Our Sister Killjoy (1977), Changes: a Love ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[